                <pb facs="0806" n="796" xml:id="pg796"/>

                <head>Appendix C to HD–122</head>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">organization committee<lb/>of
                        the<lb/>reparation commission</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Note of December 29 in Regard to
                        Granting Credits to Austria</hi></p>
                <p>We have the honor to inform you that in execution of the Resolution of the
                    Supreme Council of November 20, 1919 (H. D. 97 IV),<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d38-f1"/> the Organization Committee of the Reparation Commission
                    again examined the paragraph of its conclusions beginning with the words
                    “require immediately the Austrian Government”.</p>
                <p>The Organization Committee of the Reparation Commission agreed to propose to the
                    Supreme Council the following draft of this paragraph: <list>
                        <label>1)</label>
                        <item>Inform the Austrian Government that no granting of credits could be
                            considered if it did not agree to: <list>
                                <label><hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                                <item>Not effect, or allow to be effected, any alienation of public
                                    properties, or disposal of public authorities, even in the form
                                    of concessions or monopolies, without the consent of the
                                    Reparation Commission, and to declare null and void any
                                    alienation of this sort effected since the Armistice, November
                                    3, 1918.</item>
                                <label><hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                                <item>To take, at the request of the Organization Committee of the
                                    Reparation Commission all measures liable to prevent the
                                    alienation outside of Austria, or to other than Austrian
                                    nationals, without the consent of the Reparation Commission, of
                                    all private property if the alienation of such property would be
                                    of a nature to compromise the guarantees for credits to be
                                    opened.</item>
                            </list></item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer>B. O. of the Committee<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Interallied
                        Secretary</hi><lb/>Signature</closer>
            </div>
